# 8. Add observer-to-safety transfer results

The framework should not stop at saying an observer is required. It can state a precise sufficient condition connecting estimation error to safety margin.

Suppose \(K=\{X:b_i(X)\ge0\}\), and a full-state controller satisfies

\[
\inf_w \nabla b_i(X)\cdot f(X,k(X),w)
\ge \eta_i>0
\]

on the active boundary. If

\[
\left|
\nabla b_i(X)\cdot
\left[
f(X,k(\widehat X),w)-f(X,k(X),w)
\right]
\right|
\le L_i\|\widehat X-X\|,
\]

then the output-feedback controller is safe whenever

\[
L_i\|\widehat X-X\|\le\eta_i.
\]

This yields an empirically meaningful requirement:

\[
\text{observer error}
\le
\frac{\text{robust inward safety margin}}
{\text{closed-loop sensitivity}}.
\]

It also motivates **eroded safe sets**

\[
K^{-\varepsilon}
=
\{X\in K:\operatorname{dist}(X,K^c)\ge\varepsilon\},
\]

which may remain output-feedback viable even when the full boundary of \(K\) does not.

