# 12. Separate uncertainty from structural model discrepancy

A bounded parameter set \(\Theta\) does not cover misspecified compartments, omitted pathways, changing institutions, or unmodelled spatial leakage.

Augment the dynamics by a discrepancy term

\[
\dot X
=
F(X_t,u,w,\vartheta)+\delta_t,
\qquad
\delta_t\in\mathcal D_t.
\]

The discrepancy set may be updated from residuals, but contraction must be justified by calibration or conformal/set-membership guarantees. It must not be reduced merely because the fitted model becomes confident.

A scientifically strong standard is:

\[
\mathbb P\{\delta_t\in\mathcal D_t\ \forall t\le T\}
\ge1-\beta
\]

under a stated data-generating assumption, or a deterministic enclosure under stated bounded-error assumptions.

This permits separate reporting of:

1. process uncertainty;
2. parameter uncertainty;
3. observation error;
4. structural discrepancy;
5. implementation uncertainty.

