# 15. Introduce a multidimensional sustainability margin

The weighted-sum lemma correctly rejects unrestricted compensation, but the replacement should be explicit.

Let

\[
m(X,u)
=
\begin{bmatrix}
g_1(X)\\
\vdots\\
g_q(X)\\
s_1(X,u)-s_1^{\min}\\
\vdots\\
s_p(X,u)-s_p^{\min}
\end{bmatrix}.
\]

Safety is the cone condition

\[
m(X,u)\in\mathbb R_+^{q+p}.
\]

A scalar certificate may be defined noncompensatorily as

\[
q(X,u)=\min_i m_i(X,u),
\]

or in normalized form,

\[
q_{\mathrm{norm}}(X,u)
=
\min_i\frac{m_i(X,u)}{\sigma_i}.
\]

Then

\[
q(X,u)\ge0
\iff
m(X,u)\ge0.
\]

Weighted averages may still be used for reporting preferences, but not as logically equivalent safety certificates unless restricted-domain equivalence is proved.

