# 18. Add a minimal impossibility taxonomy

A concise theorem-oriented taxonomy would substantially sharpen the framework.

| Failure | Mathematical certificate |
|---|---|
| Material inconsistency | Moiety residual unexplained by boundary/jump flows |
| Physical infeasibility | No admissible inward action at some physical state |
| Robust infeasibility | \(\sup_u\inf_w Dg<0\) at a boundary |
| Epistemic infeasibility | Empty common safe-action intersection over \(B\) |
| Temporal infeasibility | Exit occurs before next informative review |
| Authority failure | Safe action exists but is outside \(\Gamma(B,h)\) |
| Enforcement failure | \(\mathcal E(B,h,a)\) contains unsafe realizations |
| Recovery failure | Informational capture basin is empty |
| Model-credibility failure | Claimed uncertainty set lacks coverage validation |
| Normative incompatibility | State, service, and allocation constraints have empty intersection |

This converts the broad “governability gap” into falsifiable subclaims.

