# 19. Correct several definitions in the current drafts

## Full-information viability

The present definition should explicitly distinguish favorable and robust disturbances. Use:

\[
\operatorname{RViab}^{\mathrm{full}}_T
=
\left\{
\phi_0:
\exists\Pi^{\mathrm{full}}
\ \forall(w,\vartheta),\
X(t)\in\mathcal C_X,\
u(t)\in\mathcal A(X(t),\omega(t))
\right\}.
\]

Do not use “viability” without specifying whether the uncertainty is existential, adversarial, stochastic, or fixed.

## Output-feedback viability

It should be a set of initial information states, not simply physical histories:

\[
\operatorname{ERViab}^{\mathrm{out}}_T
\subseteq
2^{\mathscr H\times\Theta}\times\mathcal H.
\]

Two identical physical histories may generate different governability conditions if the institution begins with different uncertainty sets.

## Institution-specific safety

Include universal uncertainty quantifiers:

\[
\operatorname{Safe}^{\Pi}_T
=
\left\{
(B_0,h_0):
\forall\text{ compatible uncertainties and implementations},
\ X^\Pi(t)\in\mathcal C_X
\right\}.
\]

Otherwise “safe under \(\Pi\)” is ambiguous.

## Chance constraints

For continuous-time path safety, define the event measurably and specify the probability law:

\[
\mathbb P^{\Pi,P}
\left(
X(t)\in\mathcal C_X,\
u(t)\in\mathcal A(X(t),\omega(t))
\ \forall t\in[0,T]
\right)\ge1-\alpha.
\]

Pointwise conditions

\[
\mathbb P\{X(t)\in\mathcal C_X\}\ge1-\alpha
\quad\forall t
\]

are weaker and do not imply pathwise safety.

